cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StressFold in research, please cite the software and record the version used."
title: "StressFold: measuring selection bias in backtested strategies"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-30
authors:
  - family-names: "Mirosenski"
    given-names: "Roman"
    alias: "RomanMski"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RomanMski/stressfold"
url: "https://github.com/RomanMski/stressfold"
abstract: >-
  StressFold measures how much of a backtested result came from searching a
  parameter space rather than from skill. It reports a deflated Sharpe ratio,
  the probability of backtest overfitting, and a sweep that reruns a strategy
  on resampled price histories to show what market structure the result
  depends on.
keywords:
  - backtest overfitting
  - deflated sharpe ratio
  - selection bias
  - quantitative finance
  - strategy validation
license: MIT
